---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Art from '../components/Art.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import lock from '../assets/characters/locked-cabinet.jpg';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy note · The Paperwork Engineer"
  description="What thepaperworkengineer.com knows about you: almost nothing. No cookies, no tracking."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <main id="main" class="tpe-page">
    <section aria-labelledby="p-h">
      <div class="tpe-wrap tpe-sec">
        <div class="tpe-split">
          <div class="tpe-stack">
            <p class="tpe-eyebrow">Privacy note · Last updated <time datetime="2026-11">November 2026</time></p>
            <h1 id="p-h" class="tpe-h1">What this site knows <span class="tpe-nw">about you</span></h1>
            <p class="tpe-lede">Almost nothing. Here’s the whole list, in plain words.</p>
            <ul class="tpe-list">
              <li><h2>No cookies. No tracking.</h2><p class="tpe-body">This site doesn’t use cookies, analytics, ads or tracking pixels. Fonts and images load from this site, not from Google or anyone else.</p></li>
              <li><h2>Hosting</h2><p class="tpe-body">The site runs on GitHub Pages. GitHub logs every visitor’s IP address for security, as it does for all Pages sites. I don’t have access to those logs. Details: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.</p></li>
              <li><h2>The newsletter</h2><p class="tpe-body">If you subscribe, your email address goes to Substack, which runs the newsletter. Every email has an unsubscribe link. Details: <a href="https://substack.com/privacy">Substack’s privacy policy</a>.</p></li>
              <li><h2>Booking a call</h2><p class="tpe-body">Bookings go through Calendly, which collects your name, email and anything you write in the booking form. I use those details only to prepare for and hold our call. Details: <a href="https://calendly.com/legal/privacy-notice">Calendly’s privacy notice</a>.</p></li>
              <li><h2>Social links</h2><p class="tpe-body">Links to LinkedIn, Instagram and the rest take you to those sites. Their own privacy rules apply once you’re there.</p></li>
              <li><h2>Questions or deletion</h2><p class="tpe-body">Want to know what I hold about you, or want it deleted? <a href={site.linkedin}>Message me on LinkedIn</a>{site.email && <> or email <a class="tpe-email" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></>} and I’ll sort it out.</p></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <Art src={lock} class="tpe-art" priority sizes="(min-width: 1920px) 30vw, (min-width: 66rem) min(40vw, 35rem), (min-width: 42rem) 33vw, calc(100vw - 2rem)" alt="The Paperwork Engineer with arms folded beside a padlocked filing cabinet" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
